WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- Have a seat!

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:03.351
- Thank you, thank you for having me!

00:00:03.351 --> 00:00:04.800
- Oh my gosh, you're so funny!

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.140
We haven't seen each other
since you were my manager.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:07.973
- Yes!

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:09.570
- He was my manager at
my Christmas special.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.758
- Kelly Clarkson Christmas special, yo!

00:00:11.758 --> 00:00:12.850
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.160
- I was so nervous.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.870
I told you that backstage but
I'm not an actor so I was...

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.450
And you're so funny, and I was so nervous.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.380
I was so sweaty.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.879
- You were amazing!

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:25.010
I honestly did the special to meet you

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.441
and you're just so nice and
so cool and it was like--

00:00:27.441 --> 00:00:29.511
- I couldn't believe you said yes.

00:00:29.511 --> 00:00:32.010
- And I actually got to reference...

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:33.660
We did a scene together where

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.369
I think I referenced "Walk Away".

00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:36.840
- [Kelly] You did.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.730
- I'm just having an argument
with you in character

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:39.698
as I'm just gonna

00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:40.800
♪ Walk away ♪

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.844
or whatever it was but it
was so bad they cut it.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.680
- No, it was so awesome
because it made me feel good

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.513
'cause I was like,

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:48.346
"Oh wait, no, he knows this song."

00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:49.179
(Ken laughing)

00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:50.012
He's actually like a fan.

00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:51.477
'cause everybody always is like,

00:00:51.477 --> 00:00:53.435
"Oh, I'm such a fan,"
and they don't know you.

00:00:53.435 --> 00:00:54.268
- Right, right, right (laughing).

00:00:54.268 --> 00:00:56.126
- They're like, "Yeah, that
one song, it was great."

00:00:56.126 --> 00:00:57.252
(Ken laughing)

00:00:57.252 --> 00:00:58.920
Yeah, but congrats though
you just turned 50, right?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.696
- I just turned 50 years old.

00:01:00.696 --> 00:01:01.662
(audience cheering)

00:01:01.662 --> 00:01:03.780
- That's amazing!
- Thank you!

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.613
- Two questions.

00:01:04.613 --> 00:01:06.530
- I know I don't look it, I get it,

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.010
they say black don't crack,

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.189
well, Asian don't raisin.

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:13.022
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.337
- I've actually never heard that.

00:01:17.337 --> 00:01:18.890
- Really, you've never heard that?

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:20.533
That's on my new album,

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:24.663
Asian Don't Raisin is
coming out whenever, so.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:26.928
- I've really never heard of that.

00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:27.761
- Really?

00:01:27.761 --> 00:01:28.594
Okay.

00:01:28.594 --> 00:01:29.530
- But it's true and I'm angry about it,

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:31.780
because I'm not Asian or black.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.510
And I'm just starting to look old.

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.123
- You look amazing, what
are you talking about?

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.820
- I am three years away
from 40, man, tell me,

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.160
it gets better, right?

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.660
It gets cool, right?

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:41.915
40's gonna be awesome, right?

00:01:41.915 --> 00:01:42.748
- You are,

00:01:42.748 --> 00:01:43.978
♪ Forever young ♪

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:45.111
whatever.

00:01:45.111 --> 00:01:45.944
You know what I mean?

00:01:45.944 --> 00:01:47.556
(audience clapping)

00:01:47.556 --> 00:01:48.723
You never age.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.413
- Once you turn 50, though,

00:01:50.413 --> 00:01:52.910
are you the guy on the
lawn yelling at children?

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:53.850
Are you that guy?

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.360
- Well.
- [Kelly] Does that happen?

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.897
- I'm more the guy who
just doesn't care anymore.

00:01:58.897 --> 00:02:00.640
- Oh, that hit me about

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.473
16 (laughing).

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:05.500
- No, literally, you know
you don't care where...

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.200
I mean, I know I'm wearing this suit now,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.196
I'm lookin' fly.

00:02:08.196 --> 00:02:09.029
- Lookin' fly!

00:02:09.029 --> 00:02:11.070
- But, you know you don't
care where everything I wear

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.720
is like Gap shirt, Gap jeans, Gap jacket.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.553
- [Kelly] It's comfortable.

00:02:14.553 --> 00:02:15.386
- I'm not even kidding,

00:02:15.386 --> 00:02:17.273
this was literally what I wore to work.

00:02:17.273 --> 00:02:20.050
I don't know if the camera
can get this right here.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.460
- [Kelly] First of all, great point!

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.293
- Thank you.

00:02:22.293 --> 00:02:24.679
These are Kirkland brand socks.

00:02:24.679 --> 00:02:27.260
(audience clapping and laughing)

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.387
- Not a sponsor, just a fan?

00:02:28.387 --> 00:02:31.510
- Not a sponsor, women's size six.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.220
Just, it's the only thing
that lives and breathes

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.320
on my foot toes.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.440
- On my foot toes.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.273
- Yup.

00:02:39.273 --> 00:02:40.750
- Well congrats on season
three of The Masked Singer.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:41.583
I was telling you.

00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:42.868
- Oh, thank you so much!

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:43.701
(audience clapping)

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.210
- My family, huge fans of the show,

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.686
they totally guess before y'all do.

00:02:48.686 --> 00:02:49.519
(Ken laughing)

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:50.352
They're incredible at it.

00:02:50.352 --> 00:02:51.185
So what's new this year?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.720
- First of all, it is such an honor

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.971
to be a part of an amazing family show.

00:02:57.971 --> 00:03:00.400
Families love it and it's
like, my kids love it,

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.831
Alexa and Zooey, they love it.

00:03:03.831 --> 00:03:06.330
- What are their names?

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.110
- It's so fun to bring the
family together to watch it

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:11.890
and this season is just bigger and better.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:14.990
The producers, God bless
them, they just find new ways

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.810
to reinvent themselves every year

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.560
but the talent pool is deeper,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.770
there are just more surprising reveals.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.560
It really has evolved.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.810
The show has just gotten
better as its gone along

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.760
and I'm invested into it as a fan

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:32.210
even if I wasn't on the show.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.537
It's like America's guessing
game and it's just super fun.

00:03:35.537 --> 00:03:37.837
- I love a game so I'm in, yeah.

00:03:37.837 --> 00:03:38.670
- [Ken] Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.503
- I love trying to guess.

00:03:39.503 --> 00:03:40.336
I'm not as good.

00:03:40.336 --> 00:03:41.495
My sister nails it every time.

00:03:41.495 --> 00:03:42.328
- Really?

00:03:42.328 --> 00:03:43.161
- Yes.

00:03:43.161 --> 00:03:43.994
- You're looking at a guy

00:03:43.994 --> 00:03:46.348
that's never got a guess
right in three years.

00:03:46.348 --> 00:03:48.057
- I know, you say you're
the coolest judge.

00:03:48.057 --> 00:03:50.723
- I'm the dumbest judge
on The Masked Singer.

00:03:50.723 --> 00:03:51.980
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.150
- But you have another project

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:55.310
that's actually pretty amazing,

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:56.930
Women's Cancer Research Fund, right?

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.763
- Yes.

00:03:57.763 --> 00:03:58.689
- So how did you get started in this?

00:03:58.689 --> 00:03:59.708
(Kelly and audience clapping)

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:01.180
- Thank you, yes.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.370
I'm hosting a benefit on February 27th

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.420
for the Breast Cancer Research Fund

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.160
and it's called An Unforgettable Night

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:13.670
and it is a fundraiser for
research for breast cancer.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.336
My wife, she is a breast cancer survivor

00:04:16.336 --> 00:04:17.544
(audience clapping)

00:04:17.544 --> 00:04:19.495
and she's going on 11 years.

00:04:19.495 --> 00:04:21.828
Yup, there she is right now.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:26.400
It's an honor to work
with that organization

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.700
and we're actually
honoring Renee Zellweger

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.110
for her contributions to
breast cancer research.

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.090
It's an amazing night.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.200
I was there last year and
the amount of money we raised

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.311
was just record amounts and everything,

00:04:40.311 --> 00:04:43.330
it is wonderful that everybody,

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.500
we're all using our efforts to--

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.333
- [Kelly] Your spotlight, yeah.

00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:49.430
- Yeah, the spotlight and
being a former physician,

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.700
just knowing where this
money goes and advances

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.762
in specific receptor therapy,

00:04:54.762 --> 00:04:58.620
it can make all the side effects
from chemo very tolerable,

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.100
so there's a lot of excitement,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.014
in the forefront of cancer therapy.

00:05:03.014 --> 00:05:04.400
- And I know it affects you
personally 'cause your wife

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.240
but I feel like cancer
hits home with everyone.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.040
If it's not directly, it's indirectly.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.220
Everybody knows someone, unfortunately.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.850
- Everyone knows someone
who either has cancer

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.580
or knows someone who has
been affected by cancer.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:16.630
- It's important you're
doing these benefits.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.259
It's important everyone is
stepping up and doing that.

00:05:18.259 --> 00:05:20.930
- Yeah, it's important just
to remind ourselves that

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.680
we are all cut from the same cloth

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:27.130
and that if we can do whatever we can

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.000
to help and heal each
other, that's a good thing.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:30.833
- Yeah, raise money,

00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:32.356
alleviate things, yeah, I agree with you.

00:05:32.356 --> 00:05:33.647
(audience clapping)

00:05:33.647 --> 00:05:34.480
So what can people....

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.560
What can we do to help?

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.580
Like, how can people help?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.370
- Well, you can go to the website.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.810
I believe it's called wcrfcure.org

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:46.430
and I'll put it on my social media as well

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.410
to help contribute,

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.070
but just the fact that...

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:52.201
Thank you for letting me
even talk about it right now.

00:05:52.201 --> 00:05:53.970
It's a big deal to me, so thank you.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.010
- It's a big deal to us here, too.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.320
We've actually had several stories

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:59.220
and several different
organizations on the show so far,

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:00.053
'cause it's important.

00:06:00.053 --> 00:06:01.260
It's important to eradicate it.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.070
It's important to get
there and get to a cure.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.600
- Yes, absolutely, all
forms of cancer, absolutely.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.900
- [Kelly] Yes, absolutely.

